.claude/workbench/translation/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24/chunks/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24__lecture02__lecture02-notes/010.es.tex:5:Anthropic operationalizes incidents using a multi-step checklist:
.claude/workbench/translation/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24/chunks/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24__lecture02__lecture02-notes/010.es.tex:17:Each deployment uses two playbooks—`Launch Playbook` and `Rollback Playbook`. The launch playbook enumerates gating evidence (matrix rows, telemetry dashboards, trustee review). The rollback playbook spells out evaluation metrics, check for repeated incursion, and communication plan.
.claude/workbench/translation/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24/chunks/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24__lecture02__lecture02-notes/010.es.tex:21:Metrics glossary + checklists keep tooling grounded: each number in the evidence matrix is tied to a data source, each incident follows a documented escalation path. These artifacts make evaluation defensible even under audit scrutiny.
.claude/workbench/translation/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24/chunks/talks__berkeley-llm-agents__f24__lecture03__lecture03-notes/002.es.tex:8:    \item Open source: como un «ingeniero de sistemas» que puede reescribir todo el pipeline.
